    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1157">

                <pb facs="0825" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/117.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-29T20:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Cándido Aguilar informed this office today that he had given orders for
                    proper protection Panuco-Topila district and that all Americans who have
                    requested permission to carry revolvers have been granted same. Also that he
                    will severely punish any disorders or molestation of workingmen. Admiral Mayo
                    called on Acting Governor Lara this morning and Governor Lara promised to send
                    some troops to Panuco pending arrival troops of General Aguilar. Authorities
                    manifest disposition to give necessary protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
